 ],
 "literal": "Even the calf not drinking, even in the vessel not being poured, / the sweet milk of the good cow, on the ground spilling, / neither becoming of use to me, nor being useful to my husband, / the pallor wants to consume / the beauty of my dark complexion and spotted waist!",
 "translation": "Like the sweet milk of a good cow, which is neither drunk by the calf nor collected in a vessel, but is wasted by spilling on the ground, the beauty of my dark complexion and spotted waist is of no use to me, nor does it benefit my husband; instead, the pallor of separation desires to consume it entirely.",
 "modern": "கன்றும் குடிக்காமல், பாத்திரத்திலும் சேராமல், நல்ல பசுவின் இனிமையான பால் தரையில் கொட்டி வீணாவது போல, என் கணவனுக்கும் உதவாமல், எனக்கும் பயனின்றி, தேமல் படர்ந்த என் அல்குலின் மாமை நிற அழகினைப் பசலை நோய் உண்ண விரும்புகிறது.",
 "explanation": "The heroine speaks to herself or her confidante in deep grief during her husband's absence, which belongs to the Pālai (separation) landscape. She compares her fading youth and beauty to the sweet milk of a good cow that is completely wasted. This milk is neither drunk by the calf nor gathered in a vessel for human consumption, but is simply spilled on the ground. Similarly, because her husband is away, her beauty is of no use to him, nor can she enjoy it herself. Instead, the spreading pallor of separation (pasalai) is eagerly consuming her beautiful dark complexion.",
